                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#898989' fontsize='8'>Key finding: Low comorbidity burden hospitals ($14,493) show higher payments  per discharge than high burden hospitals ($12,045) — a $2,448 gap. This  counterintuitive finding reflects specialty hospital influence, where facilities  with lower recorded comorbidity indices receive higher Medicare payments due to specialized reimbursement structures. 1,057 hospitals fall in the high burden tier.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>Data note: Comorbidity index = sum of 14 physical condition prevalences. Tiers defined by 33rd and 66th percentile thresholds of the comorbidity index.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
