                <zone h='60807' id='29' type-v2='text' w='9370' x='89971' y='38021'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontsize='8'>Key finding: High dual-eligible hospitals consistently show longer inpatient </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>stays than low dual-eligible hospitals across all behavioral health burden </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>levels (gap: 0.57 days nationally — 5.46 vs 4.89 days per discharge). </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>Notably, the gap remains relatively constant across Low, Medium, and High </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>BH burden tiers, suggesting dual-eligible status independently drives </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>utilization regardless of behavioral health burden level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>Data note: Behavioral burden index = sum of 10 behavioral condition </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontsize='8'>prevalences. Dual tier defined at median dual-eligible share (50th percentile).</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
