                  <zone h='9766' id='19' name='Payment Across Tiers' param='[federated.08yb1ib0r4lqav1fpgbsl0m72mwi].[usr:Calculation_1952790990282754:qk]' show-domain='false' show-null-ctrls='false' type-v2='filter' w='12810' x='86604' y='30859'>
                    <zone-style>
                      <format attr='border-color' value='#d4d4d4' />
                      <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
                      <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
                      <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    </zone-style>
                  </zone>
                  <zone h='58333' id='26' type-v2='text' w='12810' x='86604' y='40625'>
                    <formatted-text>
                      <run fontsize='8'>Key finding: High dual-eligible hospitals receive higher average payments per </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>discharge ($13,764) than low dual-eligible hospitals ($11,938) — a $1,826 gap. </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>This counterintuitive finding mirrors the Q2 geographic confounding effect: </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>high dual-eligible hospitals concentrate in urban areas where CMS wage index </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>adjustments increase reimbursements. The median gap is smaller ($516) suggesting </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>outlier hospitals drive the average difference. National avg dual-eligible share </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>is 25% — meaning 1 in 4 Medicare inpatients also qualifies for Medicaid.</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>Data note: Dual tier defined at median dual-eligible share. Box plots show </run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='8'>median, IQR, and whiskers at 1.5x IQR. Individual hospitals shown as dots.</run>
                    </formatted-text>
                    <zone-style>
                      <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                      <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                      <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                      <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    </zone-style>
